# Shared toolchain pin (asdf / mise). One Node version for the repo.
# - Go is NOT pinned here: go.mod's `go` directive is the only copy, and every
#   workflow reads it through `go-version-file: go.mod`. The example Dockerfile
#   builder must name the same Go; the org toolchain guard (zeroroot-ai/.github
#   check-go-toolchain.sh, run by reusable-go-ci) fails the PR when it drifts.
#   Local: `go version` must satisfy go.mod (GOTOOLCHAIN=auto downloads it).
# - Node matches the CI `setup-node` major (20) used to run the lint scripts
#   under scripts/ (stdlib-only, no npm deps). buf is a go.mod tool dependency
#   (`go tool buf`), not a node tool.
# Quality bar: docs/architecture/open-core/RESTRUCTURE-QUALITY-BARS.md §1.
#
# golangci-lint is NOT pinned here: it is built from source at the version in
# the Makefile (GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION) by the `bootstrap`/`lint` targets, so its
# embedded Go toolchain never trails go.mod's target (golangci v2 refuses to
# load a config targeting a newer Go than the binary was built with).
nodejs 20.20.2
